    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0705" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/1358</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Embassy to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <p>His Majesty’s Government deeply appreciate the action taken by the President in
                    regard to the international crisis.</p>
                <p>The two messages enclosed herein,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d673-f1"/> from the Prime
                    Minister to Herr Hitler and to Signor Mussolini will show that the action of His
                    Majesty’s Government is much on the same lines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1938-09-28">September 28,
                            1938</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d673-f1" n="1" xml:id="d673-f1-content">
                <p>Dated September 28, 1938; see <hi rendition="#italic">British Documents</hi>, 3d
                    ser., vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, docs. No. 1158 and No. 1159, p.
                    587.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
